{# The poster id is read from the database by getImages(): outside a real product it falls back to
   the placeholder, which is enough to check the box, the play button and what the click builds. #}

<div class="Story">

    <div class="Story-section">
        <h4 class="Story-title">Platform video</h4>
        <span class="Story-label">
            Nothing is requested from the platform until the button is clicked: the frame is built
            then, from the address the core handed over. The address is never assembled here.
        </span>
        <div class="max-w-2xl">
            <twig:Organisms:VideoPlayer:Base
                alt="A demonstration of the product"
                provider="youtube"
                embedUrl="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/dQw4w9WgXcQ"
                :thumbnailImageId="1"
            />
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="Story-section">
        <h4 class="Story-title">Hosted video</h4>
        <span class="Story-label">
            A file the shop serves itself: the click swaps the poster for a native player with its
            own controls. This story points at a file that does not exist, so the player shows its
            error state — what matters here is that no video tag exists before the click.
        </span>
        <div class="max-w-2xl">
            <twig:Organisms:VideoPlayer:Base
                alt="Assembling the product step by step"
                provider="file"
                fileUrl="/cache/videos/product/toolkit-story.mp4"
                :thumbnailImageId="2"
            />
        </div>
    </div>

</div>
